    "result": "I implemented `add_business_days(start, n, holidays=())` in `solution.py`, keeping the stub's signature and imports. The function validates inputs first: `start` must be a `date` and not a `datetime`, `n` must be an `int` and not a `bool`, and every holiday must be a `date` and not a `datetime`; otherwise it raises `TypeError`. Holidays are collected into a set so that membership checks are fast, and generators work because they are consumed once. For `n == 0` it returns `start` if it is a business day, otherwise it steps forward to the next one. For `n != 0` it steps one day at a time in the direction of `n`, counting only Monday–Friday dates not in the holiday set, and returns the date where the count reaches `|n|`, so `start` itself is never counted. I did not run or test the code, since shell access was not available, and I only edited `solution.py` as instructed.",
